  <Docs>
    <summary>Provides the text-to-speech engine initialization status for a .NET event handler.</summary>
    <remarks>
      <para>The status corresponds to the <see cref="T:Android.Speech.Tts.TextToSpeech.IOnInitListener" /> callback: <see cref="F:Android.Speech.Tts.OperationResult.Success" /> indicates successful initialization, and <see cref="F:Android.Speech.Tts.OperationResult.Error" /> indicates failure.</para>
      <para><format type="text/html"><a href="https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/base/+/1cdfff555f4a21f71ccc978290e2e212e2f8b168/core/java/android/speech/tts/TextToSpeech.java">Android initialization callback contract.</a> <a href="https://github.com/dotnet/java-interop/blob/92b5d471f1e0f6164fc332b1f661b472f5cf3aad/tools/generator/SourceWriters/InterfaceEventArgsClass.cs">.NET event argument storage implementation.</a></format></para>
